index=f'''{head}<title>Susie Kirchgessner — Creative Strategist, Designer, Writer & Builder</title><meta name="description" content="The multidisciplinary portfolio of Susie Kirchgessner: creative strategy, design, content, systems, and writing."></head><body>{header}<main><section class="hero wrap"><div class="eyebrow"><span class="line"></span> A multidisciplinary portfolio</div><div class="hero-grid"><h1>Susie<br><em>Kirchgessner.</em></h1><div class="hero-side"><p class="role">Creative Strategist, Designer,<br>Writer & Builder</p><p class="lead">I turn messy ideas into clear strategies, useful systems, visual stories, and things people can actually use.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button primary" href="#work">Explore My Work <span>↗</span></a><a class="button quiet" href="#about">About Me <span>↗</span></a></div></div></div><div class="hero-bottom"><span>Strategy meets storytelling meets execution.</span><a href="#work">Scroll to explore ↓</a></div></section><section class="work-section" id="work"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head"><div><p class="overline">01 / Selected work</p><h2>Ideas, made useful.</h2></div><p>Different mediums. One throughline: understand the problem, shape the story, build the thing.</p></div><div class="filters" role="group" aria-label="Filter projects">{filters}</div><div class="project-grid" id="project-grid">{cards}</div><p class="sample-note">These are sample case-study structures. Project details and evidence will be added as the portfolio is populated.</p></div></section><section class="about-section wrap" id="about"><div class="section-head compact"><p class="overline">02 / About</p><h2>A creative mind with a practical streak.</h2></div><div class="about-grid"><p class="statement">I see the connections between ideas, systems, content, design, and the person on the other side of the screen.</p><div class="about-copy"><p>My work moves across creative strategy, brand direction, content and publishing, visual design, digital products, WordPress, creator education, AI-assisted workflows, and storytelling.</p><p>I like the part where something is still messy: listening closely, finding its shape, making a plan, and carrying it through to a useful result.</p></div></div></section><section class="process-section"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-head compact"><p class="overline">03 / How I work</p><h2>Find the clear next move.</h2></div><ol class="process"><li>Explore</li><li>Clarify</li><li>Strategize</li><li>Build</li><li>Refine</li><li>Ship</li></ol></div></section><section class="focus-section wrap" id="systems"><div class="focus-label"><p class="overline">04 / AI & systems</p><h2>Tools in service of better work.</h2></div><div><p>AI is one part of my creative and strategic toolkit. I use it to support research, design context, build repeatable workflows, and turn early ideas into usable output—with judgment and revision throughout.</p><div class="text-tags"><span>LLM-assisted research</span><span>Prompt & context design</span><span>Notion & Airtable systems</span><span>Creative workflows</span></div><a class="text-link" href="/projects/ai-workflows/">Explore the sample case study ↗</a></div></section><section class="writing-section" id="writing"><div class="wrap writing-grid"><div><p class="overline">05 / Writing & storytelling</p><h2>Words belong here, too.</h2></div><div><p>Essays, blogs, newsletters, fiction, editorial work, and eventually audio: each has its own form, but all begin with curiosity and a point of view.</p><a class="button outline" href="/projects/writing-storytelling/">See the writing space ↗</a></div></div></section><section class="skills-section wrap"><div class="section-head compact"><p class="overline">06 / Skills & tools</p><h2>The working toolkit.</h2></div><div class="skills-grid"><div><h3>Strategy</h3><p>Creative strategy, content strategy, brand direction, creative direction</p></div><div><h3>Design</h3><p>Photoshop, Illustrator, InDesign, Canva, digital product design</p></div><div><h3>Web & publishing</h3><p>WordPress, content publishing, email marketing, Pinterest</p></div><div><h3>Systems</h3><p>Notion, Airtable, workflow design</p></div><div><h3>AI</h3><p>LLM workflows, prompt design, AI research, assisted creative development</p></div><div><h3>Writing</h3><p>Blogging, editorial writing, storytelling, fiction, editing</p></div></div></section><section class="contact-section" id="contact"><div class="wrap contact-grid"><div><p class="overline">07 / Contact</p><h2>Have a good<br><em>problem to solve?</em></h2></div><div><p>I’m open to creative strategy, content, education, design, and thoughtfully unusual opportunities.</p><a class="contact-link" href="mailto:hello@strategywithsusiek.com">hello@strategywithsusiek.com ↗</a><div class="contact-links" id="resume"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/susiekirchgessner/" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">LinkedIn ↗</a><a href="https://clippings.me/susiekirch" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Writing samples ↗</a><span>Resume download — add current PDF</span></div></div></div></section></main>{footer}<script src="/site.js" defer></script></body></html>'''
(root/'index.html').write_text(index)
for p in projects:
 slug,cat,title,heading,desc,tags,theme=p
